          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-test-function-lf-topology-universal-property",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The test-function topology exists as a Hausdorff locally convex vector topology, induces the prescribed topology on each $\\mathcal D_K$, and is the finest locally convex topology making all inclusions $\\mathcal D_K\\to\\mathcal D(\\Omega)$ continuous. A linear map $L:\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\to E$ to a locally convex space is continuous if and only if each restriction $L|_{\\mathcal D_K}$ is continuous. An increasing compact exhaustion whose interiors cover $\\Omega$ gives the same topology, independently of the exhaustion. Thus this is an LF topology of the complete metrizable fixed-support spaces. All these claims hold in ZF.",
